{
  "name": "Elemental Smite",
  "type": "feat",
  "_id": "U7Dl24fX93uEPyS8",
  "img": "icons/magic/symbols/elements-air-earth-fire-water.webp",
  "folder": "wq235y3tz8EbsQBF",
  "sort": 100000,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Immediately after you cast Divine Smite, you can expend one use of your Channel Divinity to invoke one of the following effects.</p><p><strong>Dao's Crush.</strong> Earth rises around the target of your Divine Smite: it has the Grappled condition (escape DC equal to your spell save DC), and while Grappled, it has the Restrained condition.</p><p><strong>Djinni's Escape.</strong> You teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet of you and take on a semi-incorporeal form until the end of your next turn. While in it, you have Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage and Immunity to the Grappled, Prone, and Restrained conditions.</p><p><strong>Efreeti's Fury.</strong> The target of your Divine Smite takes an extra 2d4 Fire damage, and fire leaps from it to another creature you can see within 30 feet of you, which also takes 2d4 Fire damage.</p><p><strong>Marid's Surge.</strong> The target of your Divine Smite and each creature of your choice in a 10-foot Emanation originating from you make a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, a creature is pushed 15 feet straight away from you and has the Prone condition.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-7rEFFviW2IQXaA6v\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Efreeti's Fury: roll the damage for each of the two creatures.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
